<https://example.org/dmo/id/adverseEffect/hypoglycaemia> a dmo:AdverseEffect ;
    rdfs:label "Hypoglycaemia" ;
    dmo:adverseEffectCode "hypoglycaemia" ;
    dmo:frequencyCategory "Common" ;
    dmo:name "Hypoglycaemia" ;
    dmo:severity "Moderate" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "However, when used incorrectly, it can result in morbidity from hypoglycaemia, excess length of stay, rebound hyperglycaemia and even DKA" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "3.5.3 Treatment of hypoglycaemia * during a VRIII\n*Defined as CBG less than 4 mmol/L" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Do not allow CBG to drop below 6 mmol/L." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Avoid hypoglycaemia by providing substrate at a steady rate for the insulin infusion" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "If the TPN is stopped for any reason this will put the patient at risk of hypoglycaemia" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "2. For CBG < 4.0 mmol/L i.e. hypoglycaemia" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Avoid hypoglycaemia (CBG <4.0 mmol/L)" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "If the CBGs have fallen below 4.0 mmol/L i.e. the patient has had a hypo, stop the VRIII and treat the hypoglycaemia." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "N.B. The half-life of intravenous insulin is very short (7-8 minutes) so the VRIII must be started as soon as possible after the CBG rises >4 mmol/L to minimise the risk of ketosis." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_09_ip_vriii> .

