    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Screening" ;
    dmo:statement "Patients with type 2 diabetes may also be prone to ketone production if unwell. We recommend ketone testing in this group of patients when presenting with acute illness." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "2. Patients with type 2 diabetes may also be prone to ketone production if unwell. We recommend ketone testing in this group of patients when presenting with acute illness." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_09_ip_vriii> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/management-of-hyperglycaemia-in-patients-receiving-tpn> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Management of Hyperglycaemia in Patients Receiving TPN" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Patients receiving TPN with elevated blood glucose" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "management-of-hyperglycaemia-in-patients-receiving-tpn" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Monitoring" ;
    dmo:statement "If the blood glucose is elevated a VRIII will be required, in which case CBG should be monitored hourly. As for all patients receiving a VRIII, these patients will require daily venous blood glucose and urea and electrolytes. In addition other biochemical tests, e.g. micronutrients etc. may be needed. Consult your local nutrition and diabetes teams." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "If the blood glucose is elevated a VRIII will be required, in which case CBG should be monitored hourly. As for all patients receiving a VRIII, these patients will require daily venous blood glucose and urea and electrolytes. In addition other biochemical tests, e.g. micronutrients etc. may be needed. Consult your local nutrition and diabetes teams." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_09_ip_vriii> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/management-of-hypoglycaemia-risk-when-stopping-tpn> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Management of Hypoglycaemia Risk When Stopping TPN" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Patients receiving TPN who have the infusion stopped" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "management-of-hypoglycaemia-risk-when-stopping-tpn" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Safety" ;
    dmo:statement "If the TPN is stopped for any reason this will put the patient at risk of hypoglycaemia. In this situation the VRIII should be discontinued and blood glucose monitored hourly until the TPN can be reinstated or other steps taken to avoid hypoglycaemia. If hypoglycaemia develops – treat according to JBDS guideline ‘The hospital management of hypoglycaemia in adults with diabetes mellitus’." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "If the TPN is stopped for any reason this will put the patient at risk of hypoglycaemia. In this situation the VRIII should be discontinued and blood glucose monitored hourly until the TPN can be reinstated or other steps taken to avoid hypoglycaemia. If hypoglycaemia develops – treat according to JBDS guideline ‘The hospital management of hypoglycaemia in adults with diabetes mellitus’." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_09_ip_vriii> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/moderate-glycaemic-control-target-bg-11-mmol-l> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "moderate glycaemic control target BG <11 mmol/L" ;
    dmo:gradingSystem "NICE" ;
    dmo:populationScope "patients with acute coronary syndrome (ACS)" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "moderate-glycaemic-control-target-bg-11-mmol-l" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Monitoring" ;
    dmo:statement "aiming for moderate glycaemic control target BG <11 mmol/L with avoidance of intensive glycaemic control and hypoglycaemia" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Regular BG monitoring is advised, aiming for moderate glycaemic control target BG <11 mmol/L with avoidance of intensive glycaemic control and hypoglycaemia" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_09_ip_vriii> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/monitoring-blood-glucose-after-initial-meal-time-bolus-with-csii> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Monitoring Blood Glucose After Initial Meal Time Bolus with CSII" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Patients who have resumed CSII after discontinuation" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "monitoring-blood-glucose-after-initial-meal-time-bolus-with-csii" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Monitoring" ;
    dmo:statement "Check the BG 2 hours after the initial meal time bolus. If the BG is >14, pump manufacturer’s hyperglycaemia guidelines should be followed. A correction should be given via the pump and glucose checked again 1 hour later. If glucose has risen or no improvement is seen, the cannula should be re-sited and the patient should be checked for ketones. This is to establish that the cannula is patent as the cannula may bend/kink on insertion, preventing insulin infusion." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Check the BG 2 hours after the initial meal time bolus. If the BG is >14, pump manufacturer’s hyperglycaemia guidelines should be followed. A correction should be given via the pump and glucose checked again 1 hour later. If glucose has risen or no improvement is seen, the cannula should be re-sited and the patient should be checked for ketones. This is to establish that the cannula is patent as the cannula may bend/kink on insertion, preventing insulin infusion." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_09_ip_vriii> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/nice-recommends-the-use-of-a-dose-adjusted-intravenous-insulin-to-prevent-uncontrolled-hyperglycaemia-bg-11-0-mmol-l-in-patients-with-acute-coronary-syndrome-acs> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "NICE recommends the use of a dose adjusted intravenous insulin to prevent uncontrolled hyperglycaemia (BG >11.0 mmol/L) in patients with acute coronary syndrome (ACS)" ;
    dmo:gradingSystem "NICE" ;
    dmo:populationScope "patients with acute coronary syndrome (ACS)" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "nice-recommends-the-use-of-a-dose-adjusted-intravenous-insulin-to-prevent-uncontrolled-hyperglycaemia-bg-11-0-mmol-l-in-patients-with-acute-coronary-syndrome-acs" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "NICE recommends the use of a dose adjusted intravenous insulin to prevent uncontrolled hyperglycaemia (BG >11.0 mmol/L) in patients with acute coronary syndrome (ACS). Regular BG monitoring is advised, aiming for moderate glycaemic control target BG <11 mmol/L with avoidance of intensive glycaemic control and hypoglycaemia" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Based on current evidence, NICE recommends the use of a dose adjusted intravenous insulin to prevent uncontrolled hyperglycaemia (BG >11.0 mmol/L) in patients with acute coronary syndrome (ACS). Regular BG monitoring is advised, aiming for moderate glycaemic control target BG <11 mmol/L with avoidance of intensive glycaemic control and hypoglycaemia" ;
